WEBVTT

00:07.290 --> 00:10.350
Koi seyo shounen shoujo tachi

00:11.020 --> 00:13.890
Kirari hitomi ni hoshi irete

00:14.600 --> 00:17.430
Umareta manma no jounetsu ga

00:18.230 --> 00:21.000
Hibana chirasu Jungle Haré nochi Guu!

00:21.840 --> 00:24.930
Mekurumeku koshitsuki MUCHO

00:25.410 --> 00:28.670
Kodomo nya kiwadoi AMIGO

00:28.910 --> 00:32.000
Kisu shitara suikomaresou

00:32.610 --> 00:35.080
Kowai mono mitasa TONIGHT

00:36.220 --> 00:38.120
Ojikeduitara dame

00:38.120 --> 00:39.850
Oshite osarete GOING

00:39.850 --> 00:41.660
Dokkiri kibun ga iine

00:41.660 --> 00:43.250
Chakkari asa made DANCING

00:43.790 --> 00:45.260
LOVE LOVE LOVE

00:45.260 --> 00:48.890
TROPICANA

00:50.630 --> 00:53.690
Yashi no kokage de tsukamaete

00:54.300 --> 00:57.240
Jirashite tokoton tokoton

00:57.910 --> 01:00.900
Gomen ne anata wa mou toriko

01:01.510 --> 01:04.600
Nigerarenai Jungle Haré nochi Guu!

01:05.250 --> 01:08.150
Koi seyo shounen shoujo tachi

01:08.850 --> 01:11.680
Kirari hitomi ni hoshi irete

01:12.350 --> 01:15.340
Umareta manma no jounetsu ga

01:15.960 --> 01:18.150
Hibana chirasu Jungle Haré nochi Guu!

01:23.880 --> 01:24.900
I'll be going now!

01:25.350 --> 01:27.010
Take care!

01:35.190 --> 01:36.990
Guu, you're coming with me to school!

01:36.990 --> 01:39.050
This is no time for you
to be doing such an old-school gag!

01:39.400 --> 01:43.330
I wanted you to feel at ease, Haré,
among all your hardships...

01:43.530 --> 01:46.930
I feel most relaxed when you don't do
anything, Guu.

01:48.370 --> 01:49.460
Yo, you there, Bro.

01:51.680 --> 01:52.270
Me?

01:52.440 --> 01:55.100
Yeah, you stylish dude.

01:57.710 --> 01:59.680
Wait! You're so modest!

01:59.750 --> 02:00.910
Don't be leaving, leaving me behind!

02:01.120 --> 02:04.090
A Big Box

02:08.830 --> 02:10.160
Do you want me for something, Mister?

02:10.530 --> 02:12.260
I have to go to school now.

02:12.360 --> 02:13.350
Something big!

02:13.760 --> 02:15.390
I need some advice from ya right now.

02:15.970 --> 02:18.640
I'm going to see an old acquaintance for the
first time in a few years...

02:18.640 --> 02:20.360
...but it ain't no fun to see them
in a normal matter, right?

02:20.800 --> 02:23.300
Oh, so it's not fun?

02:23.610 --> 02:27.510
And so, I was wondering if there was some
plan that would surprise 'em.

02:27.610 --> 02:28.600
I see...

02:29.480 --> 02:30.780
Weird!

02:31.050 --> 02:33.240
Why is he being so friendly from the first
time we meet?

02:33.320 --> 02:34.940
And this asking for advice...

02:35.050 --> 02:37.650
Why do I get the feeling there's something
behind all this?

02:37.850 --> 02:41.020
Looking at him, he has pale skin, so he's not
from around here.

02:41.160 --> 02:42.520
Did he come over from the city?

02:42.830 --> 02:44.690
That means, his old friend...

02:47.100 --> 02:48.330
...must be him.

02:48.630 --> 02:53.870
Well, they say that friends act alike, so it
wouldn't be unusual for someone that he
knows to be strange...

02:54.170 --> 02:57.340
But, I want nothing to do with it.

02:57.340 --> 02:58.500
So, you got any ideas?

02:58.880 --> 02:59.930
Eh... W-Well...

03:00.080 --> 03:02.570
I can't come up with anything like that.

03:02.650 --> 03:04.050
Don't be saying that.

03:04.210 --> 03:06.380
Ya gotta have something, anything.

03:08.790 --> 03:09.770
Stop that.

03:12.290 --> 03:15.660
Ashio, he's scared because you're acting
very suspiciously.

03:15.930 --> 03:18.090
A coat and boots in the
constantly hot jungle?

03:18.160 --> 03:19.720
She's suspicious too!

03:19.960 --> 03:22.960
That ain't so! I'm a 100% nice young guy!

03:23.130 --> 03:25.800
Then, don't hide your face,
and speak like one!

03:27.100 --> 03:28.590
Geez, senpai...

03:31.880 --> 03:33.600
Mister, your eyes are scary...

03:36.250 --> 03:37.940
That's why I told you to hide your face.

03:38.010 --> 03:39.880
Senpai, what you're saying now
is different from before.

03:39.950 --> 03:40.880
Shut up!

03:40.950 --> 03:43.680
Your face doesn't
sit well with kids and animals.

03:43.750 --> 03:45.650
I'm sorry to surprise you so much, boy.

03:45.720 --> 03:48.890
He looks the way he does,
but deep within, he's a nice guy.

03:49.030 --> 03:50.790
He's nobody suspicious, so rest assured.

03:51.190 --> 03:54.930
A nice guy? Only the suspicious kind say
things like that...

03:55.700 --> 03:58.100
Yup, yup. I'm all good.

03:58.100 --> 03:59.430
Let's be friends!

03:59.840 --> 04:02.000
He's glaring! He's really glaring at me!

04:02.070 --> 04:03.340
Guu... You know, Guu...

04:03.340 --> 04:03.970
Hm?

04:04.340 --> 04:05.430
H-Hey, Guu.

04:05.580 --> 04:06.600
Do something about this.

04:06.710 --> 04:10.680
I want to leave here peacefully,
without upsetting that guy.

04:10.680 --> 04:11.110
Sure!

04:11.510 --> 04:12.810
Thank goodness!

04:13.050 --> 04:16.250
Guu comes in handy at times like this
because nothing phases her.

04:17.320 --> 04:20.410
With that face of yours, are you sure you're
not in the wrong anime?

04:20.490 --> 04:21.420
Wrong!

04:21.690 --> 04:24.590
That was the message that boy over there
wanted me to pass along.

04:24.860 --> 04:26.120
Noo!

04:27.100 --> 04:27.500
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry...

04:27.500 --> 04:28.870
You sure say funny stuff.
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry...

04:28.870 --> 04:29.900
My stomach hurts from laughing!
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry...

04:29.900 --> 04:31.800
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry...

04:31.800 --> 04:32.360
All right.

04:32.440 --> 04:34.160
You and me are gonna be brothers from
today on, okay?

04:34.240 --> 04:35.900
It's great that you made a new friend.

04:35.970 --> 04:38.570
No, this isn't the way I wanted things to be.

04:38.740 --> 04:40.610
That's enough of that now.

04:40.680 --> 04:42.080
Can you please decide on
what to do quickly?

04:42.680 --> 04:45.010
I don't mind visiting in an ordinary manner...

04:45.080 --> 04:46.980
But you insisted
on a surprise reunion, Ashio.

04:47.050 --> 04:48.310
That's why I'm waiting here for you like this.

04:48.520 --> 04:51.720
You say that, senpai, but you rejected each
and every one of my plans.

04:51.860 --> 04:53.880
All of your plans are all screwed up!

04:54.090 --> 04:55.890
That's not true, right brother?

04:55.960 --> 04:56.820
Right?

04:57.030 --> 04:59.890
Well, um, I'm not really seeing the flow of
things here...

05:00.160 --> 05:02.100
All right! I'll tell you. So listen, listen up!

05:02.400 --> 05:04.300
Make sure you picture eveything clearly.

05:04.370 --> 05:04.920
S-Sure.

05:05.140 --> 05:08.800
This is when the target
is lounging at home as usual.

05:12.480 --> 05:15.470
And then, an old acquaintance snakes in
from the middle of the wall.

05:15.850 --> 05:17.280
Hey! Long time no see!

05:20.380 --> 05:21.480
Wouldn't you be surprised?

05:22.620 --> 05:24.920
Well, you'd be strange if you weren't
surprised by that...

05:25.060 --> 05:26.990
Right! You really get it.

05:27.060 --> 05:28.220
You've got nice feelings.

05:28.330 --> 05:29.290
Or rather...

05:29.360 --> 05:30.880
...there's something wrong with this guy.

05:31.030 --> 05:34.020
You're not one
that should be passing judgement.

05:34.460 --> 05:36.560
Don't you think it's great to bring in the
"going through the wall" gag?

05:36.630 --> 05:38.460
Nobody would expect that, right?

05:38.540 --> 05:40.700
Actually, it's impossible
for anyone to expect that.

05:41.000 --> 05:42.400
Then, how about this?

05:43.010 --> 05:46.310
Imagine net-surfing
in a relaxing moment late at night.

05:47.910 --> 05:50.900
Then an e-mail with a file attachment arrives.

05:51.280 --> 05:54.350
Wondering what it is,
you fearfully click on the file...

05:54.350 --> 05:56.750
...and an acquaintance suddenly
pops out of the computer screen!

05:57.090 --> 05:57.750
Yo!

06:00.060 --> 06:01.280
You'd be surprised, right?

06:01.390 --> 06:02.260
Huh...

06:02.360 --> 06:05.490
The point here is you'd be relieved that he
wasn't a virus!

06:05.560 --> 06:06.820
The point, huh...

06:06.900 --> 06:09.560
And, the best idea is yet to come!
Listen, listen up!

06:09.670 --> 06:10.720
There's more?

06:11.130 --> 06:13.860
The phone rings during your normal
relaxation time.

06:14.900 --> 06:16.930
"Oh, who could it be?" you wonder as you
answer the phone.

06:17.010 --> 06:18.440
Why does he sound like a girl?

06:18.440 --> 06:21.610
The caller was an old acquaintance, and
says, "It's been a while..."

06:21.610 --> 06:24.580
...and when you look outside the window,
the caller is standing right outside,
with a cell phone in hand.

06:25.010 --> 06:25.640
Yo.

06:25.720 --> 06:27.840
This one is normal.

06:28.420 --> 06:29.850
Or so you thought.

06:30.850 --> 06:32.850
But, that phone was actually a fax!

06:33.460 --> 06:35.950
And, what was being sent was the
acquaintance.

06:37.290 --> 06:37.850
Yo!

06:38.160 --> 06:39.750
H-H-Hold on just a minute there!

06:40.630 --> 06:41.860
You'd be surprised, right?

06:42.370 --> 06:44.830
Surprised or not, they're all things that are
physically impossible!

06:45.030 --> 06:47.240
Oh, in that case,
make sure to send me from the head.

06:47.240 --> 06:48.730
It'd be awfully unstylish
to be sent from the feet.

06:48.810 --> 06:50.300
So I'm the one in charge of sending!?

06:50.510 --> 06:53.270
Oh, so human civilization
has progressed that far...

06:53.710 --> 06:56.010
No, no! Don't take all this seriously!

06:56.080 --> 06:58.050
Human knowledge is so amazing...

06:58.110 --> 07:02.350
I'm telling you! Humans going through walls,
the mail, and the fax, they're all absolutely,
positively impossible!

07:02.750 --> 07:05.950
No. Humans can do anything
if they have the will to succeed.

07:06.120 --> 07:09.290
Oh, you just said a good thing!
I was slightly touched by that!

07:09.290 --> 07:12.590
That's right. It ain't right to say something's
impossible before ya try it out.

07:13.230 --> 07:14.790
Even if you've got the willpower, you can't do
something that's impossible!

07:14.860 --> 07:17.130
Don't finish your conversation with
something out of an inspirational speech!

07:19.400 --> 07:23.360
You know, if you want to surprise this
person, you can use a simpler method.

07:23.440 --> 07:23.870
Oh?

07:24.210 --> 07:28.410
You know, like you hide in a big gift box,
and when the recipient opens it...

07:29.650 --> 07:30.410
...or something like that.

07:32.880 --> 07:34.820
I don't think of such ordinary ideas.

07:34.820 --> 07:35.420
I-I'm sorry! I said too much!
I don't think of such ordinary ideas.

07:35.420 --> 07:37.440
I-I'm sorry! I said too much!

07:37.620 --> 07:38.810
Let's do that.

07:39.020 --> 07:43.050
What?! Senpai, you rejected my ideas, and
accepted a worthless idea like that?

07:43.390 --> 07:47.630
If you're prepared to complain
about my decisions, you're prepared to
accept a pay cut, right, Ashio?

07:47.700 --> 07:49.890
All right, is there a big box around here?

07:49.970 --> 07:53.540
Got to be one around here somewhere.
Oh, that's right, the box itself isn't here so
it's impossible after all...

07:53.540 --> 07:54.200
Oh, that's right, the box itself isn't here so
it's impossible after all...

07:55.210 --> 07:58.200
I just happened to have this big box with me.

07:58.540 --> 07:59.310
Want it?

07:59.310 --> 08:00.870
Oh, we can have it?

08:00.940 --> 08:03.080
Whoa, the two of us can easily fit in this!

08:03.680 --> 08:05.510
Wait, what's up with this
"I just happened to..." thing?

08:05.580 --> 08:07.050
Someone say something about it!

08:07.350 --> 08:08.510
No need to hold back.

08:08.590 --> 08:09.820
I'm so sorry to trouble you.

08:09.820 --> 08:10.840
Thanks!

08:11.020 --> 08:13.150
Wait, nobody seems to mind!

08:13.290 --> 08:15.480
I'm sorry to have delayed you.
You must be busy.

08:15.760 --> 08:16.750
Thank you.

08:16.830 --> 08:18.290
Let's play together again sometime.

08:18.760 --> 08:20.630
Yeah. See ya later.

08:21.560 --> 08:24.530
I hope there won't be a next time.

08:26.200 --> 08:28.400
They say that birds of a feather flock
together...

08:29.310 --> 08:31.270
...but having someone like that as a friend...

08:31.270 --> 08:32.670
I feel a bit sorry for him.

08:32.880 --> 08:33.810
Hm?

08:34.040 --> 08:36.670
Oh, I'm just pitying the school doctor.

08:40.380 --> 08:41.820
Ashio, carry this.

08:44.850 --> 08:45.680
Let's go.

08:45.790 --> 08:46.720
Sure.

08:54.900 --> 08:56.660
Those two were really strange...

08:56.830 --> 08:58.770
I wonder when
they're going to visit the doctor.

08:58.840 --> 09:00.430
Yeah, yeah, those strange guys.

09:00.500 --> 09:02.770
A way to meet an acquaintance...

09:03.170 --> 09:06.160
I wonder why they're so eager to surprise
their acquaintance.

09:06.340 --> 09:07.210
Really!

09:07.280 --> 09:08.340
Hey, about that...

09:08.550 --> 09:10.980
This morning, there were strange people on
their way here.

09:11.080 --> 09:13.310
Could it be a really tall woman and...

09:13.380 --> 09:14.680
...a guy with a really sculptured face.

09:14.750 --> 09:15.840
Eh? You saw them?

09:15.920 --> 09:16.650
You too, Haré?

09:16.720 --> 09:18.120
Y-Yeah. Kinda.

09:18.290 --> 09:22.020
He gave me a hot springs cake, and asked
me to think of a good idea.

09:22.160 --> 09:24.460
He gave me chocolate macadamia nuts.

09:24.690 --> 09:26.030
I got beef jerky.

09:26.300 --> 09:28.060
I got a can of shark fin soup.

09:28.230 --> 09:29.820
I got smoked salmon.

09:30.030 --> 09:31.690
I got some coffee beans from him.

09:31.900 --> 09:32.800
What about you, Haré?

09:32.900 --> 09:35.030
I'm the only one that didn't get anything!

09:35.100 --> 09:35.970
That guy with those eyelashes!

09:35.970 --> 09:37.630
I'll share half of mine with you.
That guy with those eyelashes!

09:37.810 --> 09:41.640
Well, that aside,
what country are those two from!?

09:41.710 --> 09:44.080
This looks like a world's fair of souvenirs...

09:44.680 --> 09:46.150
This is no time to be analyzing it!

09:46.350 --> 09:48.940
Those two are really planning to surprise
that school doctor!

09:49.820 --> 09:51.410
You want mine?

09:52.160 --> 09:54.990
He's not a great guy, but since I was the one
that gave them the idea...

09:55.060 --> 09:58.220
I'll feel sorry for him
if I don't warn him about all this.

09:59.230 --> 10:01.160
Pity doesn't help anyone.

10:02.570 --> 10:03.790
What do you mean?

10:03.870 --> 10:10.100
It's an old saying that means half-hearted
acts of pity or help are no good because they
just spoil someone.

10:10.340 --> 10:11.330
That's not right!

10:11.510 --> 10:14.580
It means that the world is made up of people
that support each other...

10:14.580 --> 10:18.570
...so any good acts you do now will someday
come back to you, right?

10:20.720 --> 10:21.980
Oh, return good with evil.

10:22.190 --> 10:23.980
Don't say something so ruthless.

10:24.150 --> 10:25.980
Even matters in hell depend on money.

10:26.060 --> 10:27.040
I'm telling you...

10:27.120 --> 10:29.110
Nobody will pick up your corpse
after you die.

10:29.190 --> 10:30.990
That's not even a real proverb!

10:31.330 --> 10:33.560
Those who are hated
disperse through the world.

10:33.700 --> 10:35.500
Since you understand, cut it out!

10:35.500 --> 10:36.360
Surrounded by enemies.

10:36.430 --> 10:36.960
Huh?

10:37.130 --> 10:39.070
Seven trips, eight falls,
everything is for naught.

10:39.240 --> 10:41.100
Are you by chance talking about me?

10:41.170 --> 10:42.100
Not at all.

10:42.170 --> 10:44.110
A crying face is where a bee lands.
A crying face is where a bee lands.

10:44.110 --> 10:45.370
A crying face is what Haré has.

10:45.440 --> 10:48.680
So, you are talking about me!
Ouch, ouch, ouch, ouch...

10:48.680 --> 10:48.750
Ouch, ouch, ouch, ouch...

10:48.750 --> 10:50.450
Huh? Come to think of it...
Ouch, ouch, ouch, ouch...

10:50.450 --> 10:50.650
Ouch, ouch, ouch, ouch...

10:50.650 --> 10:52.550
When I'm doing something like this, usually...
Ouch, ouch, ouch, ouch...

10:52.550 --> 10:52.840
Ouch, ouch, ouch, ouch...

10:53.280 --> 10:54.080
Shut up!

10:54.920 --> 10:56.440
Who told you that you
could make such noise!?

10:57.320 --> 10:59.190
That's what usually happens. This is strange.

11:00.060 --> 11:01.420
Hey, Doc, I'm coming in.

11:01.820 --> 11:03.050
What the hell!?

11:12.940 --> 11:13.730
Blood?

11:21.710 --> 11:27.550
Paraben, Dimethyl Hydroxytoluene,
Yellow #4, Red #226...

11:27.980 --> 11:29.750
From these ingredients...

11:30.220 --> 11:30.920
Lipstick!

11:30.920 --> 11:32.080
Don't analyze it!

11:35.120 --> 11:37.120
This is, no matter how you look at it...

11:45.030 --> 11:46.630
Grandma Dama's hair.

11:47.540 --> 11:49.440
No, this might be...

11:54.680 --> 11:56.300
...the elder's chest hair.

11:56.550 --> 11:57.510
Are you serious?

11:58.780 --> 11:59.650
Of course not.

12:01.250 --> 12:02.010
Oh, well.

12:04.750 --> 12:05.880
I'm home.

12:06.290 --> 12:07.020
Welcome home.

12:07.390 --> 12:10.660
You know, today... this morning, there were
really strange people...

12:10.660 --> 12:14.790
...and they asked me for something that I
didn't understand, and I was late for school!

12:17.970 --> 12:19.530
But, in the end...

12:19.900 --> 12:21.640
Wait, why are you here, Doc!?

12:21.640 --> 12:24.200
You're using our house as an evacuation
point again! Leave, go home right now!

12:24.710 --> 12:27.510
If you're going to get mad,
notice me earlier than when you did.

12:27.580 --> 12:29.740
Make more noise,
and your mom will wake up.

12:32.050 --> 12:33.040
A nap?

12:34.180 --> 12:35.120
Or rather...

12:35.120 --> 12:37.750
When you hide out in our house it always
causes us trouble!

12:37.750 --> 12:38.850
Go home right now!

12:38.960 --> 12:40.890
You can still yell, even when you're
whispering?

12:41.020 --> 12:44.620
In the first place, your existence is bad for
my ethics education!

12:44.790 --> 12:45.990
Don't you be saying so yourself.

12:46.060 --> 12:48.770
Geez, you come into someone else's house
without permission...

12:48.770 --> 12:50.830
That guy I met this morning, and you, Doc...

12:50.830 --> 12:53.270
...both of you are an even match when it
comes to lack of common sense!

12:53.340 --> 12:55.240
They really mean it when they say that birds
of a feather flock together.

12:55.300 --> 12:56.640
The guy you met this morning?

12:56.770 --> 12:58.500
Yeah, your friend.

12:58.810 --> 12:59.800
Who?

13:00.110 --> 13:01.270
I don't know.

13:01.380 --> 13:02.940
Maybe you'll see him if you go home.

13:03.180 --> 13:03.840
Haré.

13:04.050 --> 13:04.840
What is it?

13:05.180 --> 13:08.010
This was right next to the door.

13:09.590 --> 13:11.780
You! You brought this here, didn't you!?

13:12.120 --> 13:15.420
I don't know anything about it. It was already
here when I got here before noon.

13:15.490 --> 13:16.390
What!?

13:16.460 --> 13:20.300
Weda-chan was asleep, and I thought it
would be bad to wake her, so I've been
keeping quiet.

13:20.300 --> 13:21.190
What's your problem?

13:21.260 --> 13:24.000
What!? Then this isn't a nap,
this is just her sleeping in!

13:24.000 --> 13:26.130
She must have gone
back to sleep right after I left!

13:26.300 --> 13:28.600
I can't believe she's still so dead asleep!

13:28.670 --> 13:30.660
Hey, Mom, get up already!

13:30.740 --> 13:32.540
What's up with this big box here!?

13:33.780 --> 13:34.540
Morning.

13:35.040 --> 13:36.840
Oh, doctor, good morning.

13:36.910 --> 13:38.540
This is no longer time
to be saying "good morning"!

13:38.710 --> 13:39.980
I'm asking, what's up with this box!?

13:45.590 --> 13:47.150
No time to yawn!

13:47.420 --> 13:53.260
This box was right outside the front door a
while after you left for school with Guu.

13:53.330 --> 13:56.230
It had a letter on it, saying it was a gift...

13:56.230 --> 13:58.790
...so I thought I'd open it together with you
after you get back from school, Haré.

14:00.400 --> 14:01.340
Just as I thought.

14:01.500 --> 14:02.270
Who is it from?

14:02.440 --> 14:03.940
It didn't say.

14:03.940 --> 14:05.130
Really, who is it from?

14:05.270 --> 14:08.940
T-T-The contents of this box must be...

14:09.880 --> 14:14.320
What should I d-d-d-do, do, do, do with...

14:14.420 --> 14:15.920
Let's hurry up and open it.

14:15.920 --> 14:17.040
Wait just a minute!

14:17.220 --> 14:19.420
What? You want to open the box yourself?

14:19.420 --> 14:20.420
Then, go ahead.

14:20.420 --> 14:22.120
Haré, you really are a child.

14:22.120 --> 14:22.760
Isn't he?

14:22.760 --> 14:23.520
That's not it!

14:23.590 --> 14:25.390
Oh, all right. Go ahead, open it, Haré.

14:25.460 --> 14:26.760
Come on, open it.

14:26.830 --> 14:28.190
That's not it!

14:28.430 --> 14:32.390
If I open this box, I have a feeling there'll be
more problems in my future...

14:32.470 --> 14:34.300
Oh, I don't want to open this,
I so don't want to open this...

14:34.770 --> 14:36.470
This is rather strange for a gift.

14:36.470 --> 14:37.630
It seems like there might be people inside it.

14:38.140 --> 14:39.330
Impossible.

14:39.440 --> 14:41.380
But there'd be a problem if this was
something perishable.

14:41.540 --> 14:45.310
After all, it's been sitting out here for about
5 hours, from when Haré went to school until
when he got back.

14:46.220 --> 14:47.340
Perishable?

14:49.220 --> 14:51.350
Hurry, hurry, hurry, hurry!

14:55.690 --> 14:57.520
What? What's inside?

14:57.630 --> 14:59.430
Why? Why are they all right?

14:59.430 --> 15:00.690
He's all normal and stuff!

15:00.830 --> 15:04.630
H-He was surely in here for at least 5 hours,
yet he doesn't have a drop of sweat on him...

15:04.700 --> 15:07.290
Oh, geez! I don't know whether to open it,
or keep it shut!

15:07.400 --> 15:08.630
A lid on something that stinks.

15:08.700 --> 15:10.760
Don't go saying something so irresponsible!

15:10.840 --> 15:13.240
You help me think of a plan to solve this!

15:13.510 --> 15:15.570
Guu's ear is impervious to chants.

15:15.650 --> 15:16.610
Don't say so yourself!

15:16.680 --> 15:18.700
Oh, is this a doll?

15:18.810 --> 15:19.470
Dunno.

15:19.550 --> 15:20.520
When did he?

15:20.780 --> 15:22.650
It's rather poor taste for a gift.

15:22.790 --> 15:24.880
Eh? But isn't it interesting?

15:25.020 --> 15:27.650
Things like this speak up when you push
their tummies.

15:28.720 --> 15:30.060
H-Hello.

15:30.390 --> 15:31.920
See? See? Just as I thought!

15:32.600 --> 15:34.060
I wonder if it says anything else...

15:34.930 --> 15:35.800
Good evening.

15:36.500 --> 15:37.800
Good morning.

15:38.270 --> 15:39.960
Good evening morning.

15:40.600 --> 15:43.330
Good even- no, Hello.

15:44.240 --> 15:45.970
It doesn't speak many lines.

15:47.710 --> 15:49.940
He lost the element of surprise.

15:50.650 --> 15:53.480
This doll really has a scary face.
He has long eyelashes, too...

15:53.550 --> 15:54.350
You think so?

15:54.420 --> 15:56.820
But I know of someone that has a face that
looks like this.

15:56.890 --> 15:58.820
Could that guy's name be Ashio?

15:58.890 --> 16:01.320
That's right. Did I tell you about him, Haré?

16:01.390 --> 16:02.150
No...

16:02.360 --> 16:04.590
It's really him. Realize it already.

16:04.890 --> 16:07.560
But that's strange...
There was one more person - a woman...

16:07.830 --> 16:09.560
I wonder if there are
any other places to push...

16:09.630 --> 16:11.030
Maybe it won't speak anymore.

16:11.100 --> 16:12.500
It seems like a crappy one.

16:12.570 --> 16:14.300
Eh? You think so?

16:14.600 --> 16:16.800
Isn't there anywhere to push?

16:22.210 --> 16:23.140
Maybe here.

16:38.260 --> 16:41.630
Ojou-sama, it's been a while.
It's your maid, Bell.

16:41.900 --> 16:42.490
Huh?

16:42.970 --> 16:44.900
Oh! Terror? This must be an act of terror!

16:44.970 --> 16:49.710
Psychological attack by a political group, or
violence meant to show off a group's power!
Or, the culprit of such actions!

16:49.710 --> 16:53.140
How can this be!? Terrorists even here in the
depths of the jungle!?

16:53.140 --> 16:56.200
T-E-R-R-O-R! An act of terror!

16:56.280 --> 16:58.770
Ashio! Hurry up and protect the ojou-sama!

16:59.020 --> 16:59.780
Bell?

16:59.920 --> 17:02.040
That means, this doll...

17:03.590 --> 17:04.550
...is Ashio?

17:04.850 --> 17:06.320
Ojou-san, it's been a while.

17:06.490 --> 17:07.890
I'm sure you were surprised. Right?

17:10.160 --> 17:13.230
Geez, Ashio, you surprised me a bit...

17:13.230 --> 17:16.030
Yes, yes, we were surprised.
We were so surprised...

17:16.300 --> 17:17.490
Who the hell are these guys?

17:17.930 --> 17:20.930
They're the kids of the live-in servants that
work in my old house.

17:21.000 --> 17:23.440
They're like childhood friends of mine.

17:23.610 --> 17:25.230
Then, they might know me...

17:25.440 --> 17:27.470
And so, who in the world are you?

17:27.540 --> 17:29.570
You sure act smug in front of Ojou-sama.

17:29.750 --> 17:32.180
What's your relationship with our ojou-sama?

17:32.250 --> 17:32.820
So, I'm-I'm... I can't speak like this.

17:32.820 --> 17:35.080
So, I'm-I'm... I can't speak like this.
Whether or not you get out of this depends
on your answer.

17:35.080 --> 17:35.810
So, I'm-I'm... I can't speak like this.

17:36.390 --> 17:38.850
M-My consciousness is slipping away...

17:39.990 --> 17:40.190
Hey! Hey!

17:40.190 --> 17:42.990
Hey! Hey!
What is it? An old guy that I don't know is
calling for me...

17:42.990 --> 17:44.290
Hey! Hey!

17:45.860 --> 17:48.520
So, who are you? Tell the truth.

17:49.570 --> 17:52.630
Dammit, I was wandering between
life and death...

17:52.800 --> 17:54.640
Well, my relationship with her-

17:54.640 --> 17:55.600
He's a friend.

17:56.470 --> 17:59.530
I think she stressed the word "friend" a bit
too much just then...

17:59.640 --> 18:00.800
You're my friend, right?

18:00.940 --> 18:02.840
No, must have been my imagination.

18:08.020 --> 18:11.480
Ashio, isn't that the boy and girl that we met
and spoke with this morning?

18:11.550 --> 18:12.520
That's right.

18:12.690 --> 18:14.780
The boy must be Ojou-san's son.

18:14.860 --> 18:16.420
He looks exactly like
her when she was young.

18:16.630 --> 18:19.660
Senpai, you're so aloof
that you didn't notice...

18:19.660 --> 18:21.860
...but I knew the moment
I set eyes on him just now.

18:24.530 --> 18:25.570
Speak up earlier.

18:25.570 --> 18:26.190
Sorry.

18:31.770 --> 18:36.440
I apologize for being so rude to you this
morning, not knowing that you were our
ojou-sama's son.

18:36.510 --> 18:37.880
Eh? Oh no, I don't mind.

18:38.110 --> 18:40.880
And this young lady is Haré-sama's
schoolmate?

18:41.080 --> 18:43.350
This girl is part of our family, Bell.

18:43.590 --> 18:44.920
Oh, Ojou-sama's...

18:44.920 --> 18:47.350
That means she's the second child!?

18:47.590 --> 18:50.890
You! Did you lay your filthy hands on my
ojou-sama!?

18:50.960 --> 18:52.480
I'll kill you!!!

18:52.560 --> 18:55.830
W-Wait a minute. I just came to this village...

18:55.900 --> 18:56.800
Wait...

18:56.870 --> 18:58.100
Hey! Hey!

18:58.100 --> 19:00.270
Hey! Hey!
Oh, that old man is calling for me again...

19:00.270 --> 19:01.640
Hey! Hey!
...and there's even an old woman with him...

19:01.640 --> 19:01.930
Hey! Hey!

19:04.470 --> 19:05.840
No, no.

19:05.940 --> 19:06.500
Huh?

19:06.910 --> 19:11.510
Guu... is... not... Weda's...

19:12.820 --> 19:17.090
Guu... is... not... Weda's...

19:17.090 --> 19:19.120
Don't speak slowly on purpose!

19:19.120 --> 19:19.680
...child.

19:20.690 --> 19:22.660
Oh, oh, my, is that so?

19:22.730 --> 19:26.350
Then, this person over here is Ojou-sama's
acquaintance from the jungle...

19:26.760 --> 19:29.500
Actually, he's Dr. Clive, right?

19:29.500 --> 19:31.830
The one that looked after
Ojou-san when she was young.

19:32.070 --> 19:32.690
Eh?

19:32.770 --> 19:36.700
Senpai, you're so aloof
that you didn't notice, but I!

19:39.580 --> 19:41.940
That means, how did this girl...

19:42.310 --> 19:44.300
Guu just lives together with them.

19:44.580 --> 19:48.220
Guu, you don't have to admit that you're
sponging off us...

19:48.220 --> 19:50.520
It must be difficult for you to say.

19:50.620 --> 19:51.220
Guu...

19:51.220 --> 19:53.260
By the way,
Weda and I are romantically involved.

19:53.260 --> 19:55.420
You're just a moocher!
Don't tell such an obvious lie!

19:56.360 --> 19:58.550
Guu is always like this,
so don't worry about...

19:59.130 --> 20:01.660
To think that our ojou-sama swung that way!

20:01.660 --> 20:03.960
Eh? Does she believe things that easily!?

20:05.130 --> 20:05.960
So shocking...

20:06.040 --> 20:07.900
Don't believe it! Of course it's a lie!

20:08.300 --> 20:09.900
Weda-chan... You're serious!?

20:09.970 --> 20:13.670
Oh, geez, why is
everyone around me so dumb!?

20:13.740 --> 20:15.140
That's not really the case.

20:15.210 --> 20:17.610
Dammit! Your explanation is late,
and your voice is too low!

20:17.880 --> 20:21.870
We just live together due to certain
circumstances.

20:21.950 --> 20:23.540
Oh, is that so?

20:24.120 --> 20:25.950
Bell, what brings you guys here anyway?

20:26.060 --> 20:30.190
I don't know why they came, but I sure hope
they quickly finish whatever errand they're
here for and go home...

20:30.530 --> 20:35.120
We were given a long vacation, Ojou-sama.
So we came all the way out here to take care
of things around the house.

20:35.970 --> 20:38.660
We'll work hard. Please assign us anything.

20:38.930 --> 20:40.770
I'm so happy. Thank you, Bell.

20:41.640 --> 20:43.260
Ojou-san, I'm here, too!

20:43.510 --> 20:44.800
You're a big help!

20:46.180 --> 20:47.010
So that's that.

20:47.210 --> 20:49.140
Our best regards.

20:49.780 --> 20:51.440
They've asked for our blessing.

20:52.680 --> 20:54.250
Oh, why?

20:54.250 --> 20:58.150
Why do strange people keep gathering
around me!? Hey, tell me.

20:58.220 --> 21:00.210
Did I do something bad?

21:00.290 --> 21:02.990
Come on, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey...

21:02.990 --> 21:04.290
Want me to tell you?

21:04.660 --> 21:06.690
Yeah, W-What, what is it? Tell me, tell me!

21:14.400 --> 21:16.170
Birds of a feather...

21:17.370 --> 21:20.570
What's that supposed to mean!?

22:35.980 --> 22:36.510
NEXT EPISODE

22:36.510 --> 22:38.820
Eh? My mom's past is finally
coming out into the open!?

22:38.820 --> 22:40.850
Come to think of it,
I myself don't know much about her.

22:40.850 --> 22:43.550
Until recently, I never even thought
about the existence of my father.

22:43.550 --> 22:45.890
Huh? Maybe I'm indifferent by nature?

22:45.890 --> 22:46.290
NEXT EPISODE

22:46.290 --> 22:49.230
That reminds me,
Mom was the daughter of a rich family...

22:49.230 --> 22:51.860
I mean, she had
Ashio and Bell as well as other servants.

22:51.860 --> 22:53.930
Although, I can't picture that
from how she is now.

22:53.930 --> 22:55.400
Guu, what's with that whistle?

22:55.400 --> 22:57.530
You want me to blow on it? Oh, I wonder
what kind of sound it makes.

22:57.530 --> 22:59.000
Hey, who did you take that from!?

22:59.500 --> 23:00.540
Next episode of Haré+Guu: BOO!

23:00.540 --> 23:02.740
Next episode of Haré+Guu: BOO!

23:02.740 --> 23:05.070
Wait, the episode title is too short!

23:05.830 --> 23:05.830
BOO!
